# Native Toolbox migration

REQ-01: Central scanners use exec arrays, no local fallback or consumer lock.
REQ-02: Preserve product policies, reports, source integrity and credential privacy.
REQ-03: Real operation requires centrally active qualified images and valid data.

- AC-01 → REQ-01: Wrapper discovery, alias mapping and native report transport pass contract tests.
- AC-02 → REQ-02: Diagnostic failures, incomplete reports, missing inventory, source changes and secret metadata are rejected.
- AC-03 → REQ-03: All scanner operations, cancellation/concurrency and age policies are qualified with real Docker.

Operational completion successor: the current criteria additionally require public
snapshot-bound origin/identity/data timestamps, unchanged age enforcement, explicit
RustSec update with integrity/offline consumption, qualified active central scanner
revisions, and a traceable real operational matrix. Include clean/known findings,
invalid options/execution failures; report absence/truncation/malformed/incompatible
schemas and empty coverage; missing/corrupt/stale/inconsistent data; prepare/publish/
select/update/recover; concurrent runs, real cancellation/resource cleanup and source
hash preservation. Define fixture oracles before execution. Internal simulated tests
cannot substitute for public Ox/Docker execution. All existing gates remain.

## Consumer documentation alignment — 2026-11-09

REQ-01/02 successor: discovery remains TOOLBOX_BIN/PATH, native tokens and exit
codes are forwarded unchanged. SELinux relabel selection must be explicit in
the caller environment; unset/empty must not become shared implicitly. Keep the
existing Ox empty-TOOLBOX_BIN rejection and Bash floor documented as local guards.
No schema-1 lock, STIC dispatcher, private import or direct tools/volume access
is introduced. AC-01/02 include this caller-controlled environment contract;
the former automatic shared default is superseded. AC-03 still requires real
consumer qualification, independent of platform documentation/active inventory.
